      "text": "Autonomous Vacuum Robot\nProject System Overview",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "w6_USMAbyzpse2-Vl_Nym",
      "originalText": "Autonomous Vacuum Robot Project System Overview",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "43FTOv1PvwUybUanezazH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -535.8017642292656,
      "y": 170.54820629462841,
      "width": 666,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 199782673,
      "version": 773,
      "versionNonce": 880668928,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785039156731,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High-Level Compute Unit: Raspberry Pi (Used for high compute tasks like\nML models and maybe GPS)\n\nReal-Time Microcontroller: ESP32-S3 (Used for low level controls such as\nsensors, motors, interrupts, etc.)\n\nDrive Actuation: \n- Option 1: BLDC from old hoverboard (Requires ESCs for each one) More\npower efficient\n- Option 2: Brushed DC motors (Easier to use, more power hungry)\n\nCutting System: A high-RPM brushed DC motor\n\nVision & Perception: A camera module for AI object detection and visual\nodometry.\n\nLocalization: GPS module\n\nInertial Sensors: An IMU (Accelerometer and Gyroscope) \n\nProximity Sensors: IR sensors\n\nPower Distribution: A main battery pack, and buck converters to supply\nstable 5V and 3.3V logic power.\n\nSafety Hardware: ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High-Level Compute Unit: Raspberry Pi (Used for high compute tasks like ML models and maybe GPS)\n\nReal-Time Microcontroller: ESP32-S3 (Used for low level controls such as sensors, motors, interrupts, etc.)\n\nDrive Actuation: \n- Option 1: BLDC from old hoverboard (Requires ESCs for each one) More power efficient\n- Option 2: Brushed DC motors (Easier to use, more power hungry)\n\nCutting System: A high-RPM brushed DC motor\n\nVision & Perception: A camera module for AI object detection and visual odometry.\n\nLocalization: GPS module\n\nInertial Sensors: An IMU (Accelerometer and Gyroscope) \n\nProximity Sensors: IR sensors\n\nPower Distribution: A main battery pack, and buck converters to supply stable 5V and 3.3V logic power.\n\nSafety Hardware: ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
